WEBVTT

00:06.048 --> 00:07.757
[dramatic music playing]

00:07.758 --> 00:09.008
[Silvermane] Gonna meet a new supplier

00:09.009 --> 00:10.927
- at the docks tomorrow.
- It's not smart

00:10.928 --> 00:13.972
for you to go out in public
till we know who tried to take you out.

00:13.973 --> 00:15.223
You were saying Flint's your bodyguard.

00:15.224 --> 00:17.016
He protects me, and he's loyal.

00:17.017 --> 00:18.309
Are we gonna talk about the fact

00:18.310 --> 00:19.644
that he turned into some kind
of sand monster?

00:19.645 --> 00:22.897
[Cat] Started about six months ago,
and it's been getting worse.

00:22.898 --> 00:24.733
This little guy right over here: Addison.

00:24.734 --> 00:25.817
Can't say I've ever seen him.

00:25.818 --> 00:28.361
[Ben] He's the guy that burned down
Silvermane's mansion.

00:28.362 --> 00:30.739
[Robbie] I am a reporter working a story
on James Addison's death.

00:30.740 --> 00:33.116
- Jimmy's dead?
- He burned down the wrong house.

00:33.117 --> 00:35.076
I don't know who hired him.
His wife might.

00:35.077 --> 00:38.621
I got a hunch that you wouldn't want
the city's most ruthless gangster knowing

00:38.622 --> 00:41.666
that the money someone paid
your husband to kill him

00:41.667 --> 00:44.878
was being spent on lobster
and designer clothes.

00:44.879 --> 00:46.671
- Mister...?
- Carmedy.

00:46.672 --> 00:48.798
Okay, Carmedy,
my rate's ten dollars a day plus--

00:48.799 --> 00:50.258
- But you'll get pictures.
- [Janet] Am I crazy

00:50.259 --> 00:53.052
- or is that the goddamn mayor of New York?
- [Robbie] Cops had an ambush

00:53.053 --> 00:54.846
set up for Silvermane at the docks.

00:54.847 --> 00:56.890
Someone gave them a tip
about a booze exchange.

00:56.891 --> 00:58.141
Cops were all set to catch the man himself

00:58.142 --> 01:00.685
- in the act, but Silvermane never showed.
- [yelling]

01:00.686 --> 01:03.230
What the hell did I just do?

01:05.983 --> 01:08.986
[desk scraping on floor]

01:12.031 --> 01:13.656
[Janet] So it's really settled?

01:13.657 --> 01:15.617
I'm not a fan of constant redecorating.

01:15.618 --> 01:16.826
I handled it.

01:16.827 --> 01:19.162
Silvermane won't be back around here.

01:19.163 --> 01:22.373
You know, this would go quicker
if either of you pitched in.

01:22.374 --> 01:23.458
- [grunts]
- [Robbie] Oh.

01:23.459 --> 01:25.502
- Oh, you needed help with that?
- [grunts]

01:25.503 --> 01:26.878
Seemed like a one-man job.

01:26.879 --> 01:28.421
Can't be that easy, can it?

01:28.422 --> 01:30.507
Not that I don't believe you, but--

01:30.508 --> 01:32.634
No, no. This was like that before.

01:32.635 --> 01:36.137
I am not talking about the desk
and you know it.

01:36.138 --> 01:38.598
[sighs] God.

01:38.599 --> 01:41.309
Imagine surviving a war
just to be killed at home.

01:41.310 --> 01:43.144
Addison didn't die a banker.

01:43.145 --> 01:44.813
I mean, the guy
torched things for a living.

01:44.814 --> 01:47.482
Besides, his wife knew
exactly what he was up to.

01:47.483 --> 01:51.194
She seemed to be doing just fine
living it up at the Geoffrey Hotel.

01:51.195 --> 01:52.904
Well, who wouldn't?

01:52.905 --> 01:54.698
[Robbie] Son of a bitch.

01:55.699 --> 01:57.492
I met this guy at the Hooverville.

01:57.493 --> 02:00.370
He's the one who pointed me
to Addison's widow.

02:00.371 --> 02:03.832
So he knows both Addison and Flint Marko.

02:03.833 --> 02:07.210
Two men with weird powers all of a sudden.
What are the chances?

02:07.211 --> 02:08.461
Exactly.

02:08.462 --> 02:09.963
I'm gonna go find this guy again,

02:09.964 --> 02:11.632
ask him some more questions.

02:13.092 --> 02:14.300
[door closes]

02:14.301 --> 02:16.553
What are you thinking about over there?

02:16.554 --> 02:20.348
I'm thinking I want you to check
if those three were ever POWs.

02:20.349 --> 02:22.100
Our units were segregated.

02:22.101 --> 02:26.020
So this guy couldn't have served directly
with Addison and Flint.

02:26.021 --> 02:27.439
So how come
they're all in the same picture?

02:29.817 --> 02:32.819
You know, sometimes I think
you forget I do this for a living.

02:32.820 --> 02:34.195
Mm. Can't imagine why.

02:34.196 --> 02:36.406
[knocking]

02:36.407 --> 02:38.409
- [tense music playing]
- [creaking]

02:39.785 --> 02:41.203
Ben Reilly?

02:45.416 --> 02:47.418
I come in peace.

02:48.878 --> 02:50.461
Finn Byrne.

02:50.462 --> 02:53.631
We haven't been formally introduced,
but...

02:53.632 --> 02:55.842
- we have someone in common.
- [Ben] In that case,

02:55.843 --> 02:57.927
uh, welcome?

02:57.928 --> 02:59.178
What happened to your muscle?

02:59.179 --> 03:00.972
Couldn't find a woman to push around?

03:00.973 --> 03:03.684
I believe you owe the lady an apology.

03:08.939 --> 03:11.025
Come on, Reilly. I've got a job for you.

03:14.153 --> 03:16.155
[creaking]

03:20.409 --> 03:22.577
I'll take that apology now.

03:22.578 --> 03:24.288
[grunts]

03:25.998 --> 03:27.916
Why me?

03:27.917 --> 03:31.002
Why not, uh, Winston?

03:31.003 --> 03:32.629
Or one of your other guys?

03:32.630 --> 03:36.007
I have Winston looking into
where this Addison boy came from.

03:36.008 --> 03:37.634
Maybe there are others like him.

03:37.635 --> 03:40.136
After me little run-in
with your pal The Spider,

03:40.137 --> 03:43.556
I really see the value
of having friends with superpowers.

03:43.557 --> 03:44.767
Oh, yeah?

03:46.644 --> 03:48.478
[groans]

03:48.479 --> 03:52.482
All right, now. I need your help
with a rat problem.

03:52.483 --> 03:56.903
You see, somebody sent Addison
to burn down my house.

03:56.904 --> 04:01.616
And I'm assuming the same somebody tipped
off the cops about my booze shipment.

04:01.617 --> 04:02.700
Got any leads?

04:02.701 --> 04:05.162
You know, it's probably someone
on the inside.

04:06.330 --> 04:07.413
[sighs]

04:07.414 --> 04:09.415
I thought it might be a guy on my payroll.

04:09.416 --> 04:10.917
Flint Marko.

04:10.918 --> 04:13.878
He's been acting strange lately, too.

04:13.879 --> 04:16.381
But he didn't know
about the shipment, so...

04:16.382 --> 04:18.716
he's either in the clear

04:18.717 --> 04:20.970
or dead at the hands of the rat.

04:22.805 --> 04:25.723
I want you to find out who it is.

04:25.724 --> 04:28.142
Start with the police raid.

04:28.143 --> 04:30.353
Someone always gets paid.

04:30.354 --> 04:33.232
But the only thing
you can trust is human nature.

04:35.317 --> 04:37.068
[groans] Jesus. [sniffs]

04:37.069 --> 04:39.112
Remember,

04:39.113 --> 04:40.739
people lie, Reilly.

04:42.241 --> 04:44.785
Only money tells the truth.

04:45.869 --> 04:47.496
A retainer.

04:48.580 --> 04:51.083
There'll be a bonus if you finish the job.

04:54.795 --> 04:56.421
- [door closes]
- So that's how you fixed it--

04:56.422 --> 04:57.630
we work for him now?

04:57.631 --> 04:59.757
Getting paid is better
than getting murdered.

04:59.758 --> 05:02.468
Hard to argue with that.

05:02.469 --> 05:04.679
"People lie. Only money tells the truth."

05:04.680 --> 05:05.763
The hell does that mean?

05:05.764 --> 05:08.057
Must be something
rich people say at cocktail parties.

05:08.058 --> 05:09.226
Not that I'll ever know.

05:10.227 --> 05:11.729
Wait a minute.

05:12.938 --> 05:14.355
What?

05:14.356 --> 05:16.066
You didn't know they made bills that big?

05:18.068 --> 05:19.610
I heard a rumor there's even 100.

05:19.611 --> 05:23.281
Crafty bastard marks all of his bills.

05:23.282 --> 05:25.575
Do we still have any of that money
from Cat Hardy?

05:25.576 --> 05:27.368
We ought to.

05:27.369 --> 05:30.329
Unless you've been sneaking off
to gamble it on horses.

05:30.330 --> 05:31.914
- Here.
- He's marking mine.

05:31.915 --> 05:33.542
He's probably marking hers.

05:35.878 --> 05:36.961
Anything?

05:36.962 --> 05:38.422
[Ben] Bingo.

05:43.385 --> 05:45.387
[♪ Kirby sings "Saving Grace"]

05:52.728 --> 05:55.396
♪ The colors fading from the photograph ♪

05:55.397 --> 05:57.148
♪ I could tell the story ♪

05:57.149 --> 05:59.817
♪ but still you wouldn't know the half ♪

05:59.818 --> 06:02.612
♪ This love was brought to life
from shards of glass ♪

06:02.613 --> 06:04.697
♪ When you kiss me there's a shifting ♪

06:04.698 --> 06:07.158
♪ in the sepia tone ♪

06:07.159 --> 06:10.369
♪ Can't escape the madness,
baby, magnetism ♪

06:10.370 --> 06:13.706
♪ Run away but something
pulls me back into it ♪

06:13.707 --> 06:16.834
♪ Lately I've been staring
at a broken mirror ♪

06:16.835 --> 06:20.296
♪ Needing someone to call my own ♪

06:20.297 --> 06:23.508
♪ Hey, lover ♪

06:23.509 --> 06:26.385
♪ I need someone to save me now ♪

06:26.386 --> 06:28.638
♪ from all the pain ♪

06:28.639 --> 06:31.099
♪ I suffer ♪

06:31.100 --> 06:33.935
♪ and the heavy world
that weighs me down ♪

06:33.936 --> 06:37.480
♪ 'Cause the world ain't sweet ♪

06:37.481 --> 06:39.857
♪ It's bitter to taste ♪

06:39.858 --> 06:41.234
♪ But you could be ♪

06:41.235 --> 06:44.446
♪ my saving grace ♪

07:05.801 --> 07:07.803
[song ends]

07:10.264 --> 07:13.933
- Newspapers! Come get your newspapers!
- [indistinct chatter]

07:13.934 --> 07:17.812
Seven police injured
in wild liquor raid on the docks.

07:17.813 --> 07:19.814
[continues indistinctly]

07:19.815 --> 07:21.357
Newspapers!

07:21.358 --> 07:24.110
- Come get your newspapers.
- [Ben muttering]

07:24.111 --> 07:25.403
That one. That one.

07:25.404 --> 07:27.947
[♪ Benny Goodman plays
"All the Cats Join In"]

07:27.948 --> 07:29.950
[clearing throat]

07:35.455 --> 07:37.290
[coughing loudly]

07:37.291 --> 07:38.791
[groans]

07:38.792 --> 07:40.001
Are you hurt, sir?

07:40.002 --> 07:42.336
Years ago.
Caught a slug in the line of duty,

07:42.337 --> 07:45.214
and your good colleagues
at this very hospital saved my leg.

07:45.215 --> 07:47.592
God bless you all for the service
you provide this city.

07:47.593 --> 07:49.552
What's your name, sweetheart?

07:49.553 --> 07:52.513
Officer Batnick with
the Patrolman's Benevolent Association.

07:52.514 --> 07:54.432
Can I trouble you
for the room numbers of the boys

07:54.433 --> 07:56.100
that came in from last night's raid?

07:56.101 --> 07:57.226
Patrolman Jones

07:57.227 --> 07:58.728
- is right behind you, honey.
- Oh, thank you.

07:58.729 --> 08:00.731
♪ ♪

08:03.400 --> 08:04.775
- [door closes]
- Patrolman Jones.

08:04.776 --> 08:07.236
Officer Batnick
with the Benevolent Association.

08:07.237 --> 08:09.405
Quite the scene
you walked into last night.

08:09.406 --> 08:10.781
Raiding the Silvermane shipment.

08:10.782 --> 08:11.991
You're a very brave man.

08:11.992 --> 08:13.117
Doesn't feel like it.

08:13.118 --> 08:15.119
Now, I'm here on behalf of the union

08:15.120 --> 08:17.455
to ensure
that our city's esteemed officers

08:17.456 --> 08:19.165
are properly compensated
for their injuries.

08:19.166 --> 08:22.418
After all, a patrolman only goes
where he's told, right?

08:22.419 --> 08:24.754
Glad someone understands how it works.

08:24.755 --> 08:26.464
You got no choice in the matter.

08:26.465 --> 08:27.757
Been there, see?

08:27.758 --> 08:28.966
Orders are orders.

08:28.967 --> 08:30.551
See?

08:30.552 --> 08:32.804
So who told you where to go?

08:33.847 --> 08:35.223
Sergeant Miller.

08:35.224 --> 08:37.558
- [lighter flicks]
- You know,

08:37.559 --> 08:39.727
when things go wrong in the field,

08:39.728 --> 08:44.148
the higher-ups wind up carrying the can
for the injuries to their men.

08:44.149 --> 08:47.610
Friend to friend, you could be in
for a little trouble down the road.

08:47.611 --> 08:49.571
Especially with guys like Jones.

08:50.656 --> 08:51.739
Jones?

08:51.740 --> 08:53.032
What the hell did Jones say?

08:53.033 --> 08:55.493
These raids,
they're meant to take weeks of prep.

08:55.494 --> 08:57.203
All we got was a measly couple hours.

08:57.204 --> 08:58.788
Pinning it on me is bullshit.

08:58.789 --> 09:01.332
If they want to blame anyone,
you should be talking to--

09:01.333 --> 09:02.500
Lieutenant Dunn.

09:02.501 --> 09:05.503
Let's just call it what it was,
a total shit show.

09:05.504 --> 09:09.090
Brave men sent to ambush
our city's toughest mobster

09:09.091 --> 09:12.176
with little time or information
now lay injured all over this hospital.

09:12.177 --> 09:13.427
Does that sound fair to them?

09:13.428 --> 09:15.429
I get orders like everybody else.

09:15.430 --> 09:17.306
Think you can say no
to the chief of police?

09:17.307 --> 09:18.391
Like to see you try.

09:18.392 --> 09:20.643
Do I need to remind you
that you're lying on your stomach

09:20.644 --> 09:22.979
with a bullet stuck in your ass?!

09:22.980 --> 09:25.773
When the chief tells you these orders
came straight from Mayor Morris,

09:25.774 --> 09:27.650
there are no questions left to ask.

09:27.651 --> 09:30.112
The mayor himself, huh?

09:32.906 --> 09:35.116
It's no good. It's broken.

09:35.117 --> 09:37.243
Two payphones down this morning,

09:37.244 --> 09:39.913
this one and the one across
from the delicatessen.

09:40.998 --> 09:42.623
If it ain't one thing, it's another.

09:42.624 --> 09:43.708
[chuckles] Yeah.

09:43.709 --> 09:45.835
I tell you, when Harriet told me
Gimbels was hiring,

09:45.836 --> 09:47.086
I raced down here.

09:47.087 --> 09:48.546
Didn't even stop to change my stockings.

09:48.547 --> 09:51.507
And then I got on the subway
and the guy goes, "Ten cents."

09:51.508 --> 09:52.591
- Get out of--
- [phone rings]

09:52.592 --> 09:54.302
[picks up phone]

09:54.303 --> 09:56.095
Hello? Okay.

09:56.096 --> 09:58.180
756 West 57th.

09:58.181 --> 09:59.975
Got it. Thanks, Janet.

10:04.438 --> 10:05.439
I lied.

10:08.025 --> 10:10.027
[mysterious music playing]

10:11.278 --> 10:12.945
[Robbie] Scuse me. Scuse me, ma'am.

10:12.946 --> 10:14.947
- Ma'am, a moment of your time?
- [dog barking in distance]

10:14.948 --> 10:16.950
[indistinct chatter]

10:25.500 --> 10:26.667
Say, brother, you seen...

10:26.668 --> 10:28.879
big Black motherfucker about this tall?

10:30.547 --> 10:32.089
[whistle blowing]

10:32.090 --> 10:33.382
On authority of Mayor Morris,

10:33.383 --> 10:35.176
this illegal camp's to be cleared!

10:35.177 --> 10:36.594
[indistinct shouting]

10:36.595 --> 10:37.887
Vacate immediately!

10:37.888 --> 10:40.015
- [shouting]
- Go!

10:43.226 --> 10:45.186
[shouting]

10:45.187 --> 10:46.563
- Get over here!
- [grunting]

10:48.315 --> 10:50.149
[shouting]

10:50.150 --> 10:51.150
Get on the ground!

10:51.151 --> 10:52.819
[groaning]

10:53.612 --> 10:54.945
[woman screaming]

10:54.946 --> 10:56.197
Stop!

10:56.198 --> 10:58.116
Let go of me. Lonnie!

10:59.368 --> 11:01.410
Help me! Lonnie!

11:01.411 --> 11:02.995
Hey. Hey! Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!

11:02.996 --> 11:04.622
Leave her be, now. Let her go.
We're all leaving.

11:04.623 --> 11:06.458
- [yells]
- [Lonnie groans]

11:07.542 --> 11:09.126
- [yells]
- [groans]

11:09.127 --> 11:11.671
[tense music playing]

11:14.049 --> 11:16.093
[shuddering]

11:18.220 --> 11:19.638
[grunts]

11:20.180 --> 11:21.639
- [grunts]
- [groans]

11:21.640 --> 11:24.226
- [indistinct shouting]
- [man] He's a monster.

11:26.103 --> 11:27.144
Shit.

11:27.145 --> 11:29.313
I told you to get ou-- [grunting]

11:29.314 --> 11:30.565
What the hell?

11:31.566 --> 11:32.734
[grunts]

11:34.111 --> 11:35.987
[man] There's another one!

11:39.533 --> 11:41.075
- [grunts]
- I'm a reporter!

11:41.076 --> 11:42.576
- I'm with the Bugle.
- Who cares?

11:42.577 --> 11:43.536
- [whimpers]
- [grunts]

11:43.537 --> 11:44.579
- [yells]
- [grunts]

11:46.206 --> 11:48.124
- Take it easy now.
- Get him!

11:48.125 --> 11:50.544
- [grunting]
- [groaning]

11:52.379 --> 11:54.797
[grunting]

11:54.798 --> 11:55.756
[yells]

11:55.757 --> 11:57.174
[grunts loudly]

11:57.175 --> 11:58.802
[grunting]

12:02.681 --> 12:05.224
[breathing heavily]

12:05.225 --> 12:07.227
[horn honking in distance]

12:10.522 --> 12:11.856
- Hey.
- [snapping]

12:11.857 --> 12:14.692
I'm looking for a guy. Carmedy.

12:14.693 --> 12:15.776
You know him?

12:15.777 --> 12:17.361
Immense. Unctuous.

12:17.362 --> 12:19.113
More pinniped than human.

12:19.114 --> 12:21.240
Pinni-ped?

12:21.241 --> 12:23.200
He's so pinniped-like,
you wouldn't believe it.

12:23.201 --> 12:24.161
Mm.

12:26.621 --> 12:28.414
He's a big guy.

12:28.415 --> 12:29.874
Smells like sauerkraut.

12:29.875 --> 12:30.958
Well?

12:30.959 --> 12:33.002
You're talking about Hicks.

12:33.003 --> 12:34.753
Apartment four.

12:34.754 --> 12:36.006
[chuckling]

12:37.007 --> 12:38.967
Temperance begins with faith.

12:40.427 --> 12:41.760
[groans]

12:41.761 --> 12:43.221
[knocking]

12:45.474 --> 12:47.475
- [creaking]
- Oh, no.

12:47.476 --> 12:48.684
No. [grunts]

12:48.685 --> 12:51.061
No. Ow!

12:51.062 --> 12:52.396
Ow! [grunts]

12:52.397 --> 12:53.481
Ow!

12:53.482 --> 12:54.608
[grunts] Ow.

12:55.609 --> 12:56.692
[groans]

12:56.693 --> 12:58.360
Gosh, I hope your arm's okay.

12:58.361 --> 13:00.112
But closing a door on a guy--

13:00.113 --> 13:01.697
is that how you treat a friend?

13:01.698 --> 13:03.699
That's not what we are.

13:03.700 --> 13:05.075
And here I thought
we could braid each other's hair.

13:05.076 --> 13:07.036
Now, I've got a few questions.

13:07.037 --> 13:08.120
Be a good boy

13:08.121 --> 13:10.206
- and I'll pay you for your trouble.
- [sighs]

13:10.207 --> 13:12.041
- Well, go on then.
- Who hired you

13:12.042 --> 13:14.210
to get those photos
of the mayor and Cat Hardy?

13:14.211 --> 13:15.586
Nobody hired me.

13:15.587 --> 13:17.046
I'm a smut merchant.

13:17.047 --> 13:19.590
Mayor cheats on wife with lounge singer?

13:19.591 --> 13:20.883
During an election?

13:20.884 --> 13:23.219
Anybody would tell you that's a doozy.

13:23.220 --> 13:24.970
Would've gotten them myself, too, but...

13:24.971 --> 13:26.055
[knocking]

13:26.056 --> 13:28.224
How'd you know it was happening?

13:28.225 --> 13:31.352
I got a tip from Morris's office
that he scheduled a meeting with the girl.

13:31.353 --> 13:32.728
He called her?

13:32.729 --> 13:34.480
She called him.

13:34.481 --> 13:35.648
I'd meet with her, too. Wouldn't you?

13:35.649 --> 13:37.900
[muffled pulsing, warbling]

13:37.901 --> 13:39.361
[Carmedy speaks indistinctly]

13:40.445 --> 13:42.655
I thought it'd be a gold mine.

13:42.656 --> 13:44.323
Sell 'em to the papers, you know,

13:44.324 --> 13:45.950
or-or the mayor himself.

13:45.951 --> 13:47.868
Could get out of this shithole.

13:47.869 --> 13:49.162
Here we are.

13:51.498 --> 13:53.374
Is there a back way out of here?

13:53.375 --> 13:55.293
[tense music playing]

13:59.965 --> 14:01.674
[lock turns]

14:01.675 --> 14:03.425
[♪ Dinah Shore sings "Dearly Beloved"]

14:03.426 --> 14:04.552
Ever heard of a telephone?

14:04.553 --> 14:06.762
Trying to save a nickel.

14:06.763 --> 14:08.764
Handsome and thrifty.

14:08.765 --> 14:10.432
Is he thirsty, too?

14:10.433 --> 14:12.644
I won't say no.

14:13.728 --> 14:15.437
♪ How clearly ♪

14:15.438 --> 14:17.399
♪ I see ♪

14:18.400 --> 14:20.901
♪ Somewhere in heaven ♪

14:20.902 --> 14:22.027
[grunts]

14:22.028 --> 14:25.282
♪ you were fashioned for me ♪

14:27.450 --> 14:28.534
♪ Angel eyes...

14:28.535 --> 14:30.119
It's a bit much, isn't it?

14:30.120 --> 14:31.829
Doesn't feel like you.

14:31.830 --> 14:34.039
I imagined something with a bit more...

14:34.040 --> 14:35.458
- edge.
- Ah.

14:36.459 --> 14:38.794
So we're imagining things now?

14:38.795 --> 14:40.797
Find me someone who wouldn't.

14:42.757 --> 14:43.882
[sighs]

14:43.883 --> 14:45.676
So...

14:45.677 --> 14:47.595
have you found Flint?

14:47.596 --> 14:50.973
Working a few leads,
but nothing, uh, concrete.

14:50.974 --> 14:53.892
Could've said that
before I got you the drink.

14:53.893 --> 14:55.478
I can always find a reason to linger.

14:56.646 --> 14:58.689
Fact is, I had to take a pause on Flint.

14:58.690 --> 15:02.861
Silvermane turned up today
and hired me to find a rat in his crew.

15:06.865 --> 15:08.866
You didn't like hearing that.

15:08.867 --> 15:10.993
The part where you're not doing the job
I hired you for?

15:10.994 --> 15:13.454
Or the part where you're working
for Silvermane?

15:13.455 --> 15:15.040
I don't like either.

15:16.374 --> 15:19.543
You see, this place doesn't feel like me.

15:19.544 --> 15:21.128
Because it's not mine.

15:21.129 --> 15:23.797
There is nothing Silvermane didn't choose.

15:23.798 --> 15:26.091
And if he gave it to me,

15:26.092 --> 15:27.843
then he can take it all away.

15:27.844 --> 15:29.928
And then some.

15:29.929 --> 15:32.890
Any chance your boy Flint's
involved in betraying him

15:32.891 --> 15:34.224
and that's why he disappeared?

15:34.225 --> 15:36.143
No, Flint is loyal to a fault.

15:36.144 --> 15:37.936
- What about the mayor?
- What about him?

15:37.937 --> 15:39.647
Booze is Silvermane's bread and butter.

15:39.648 --> 15:42.107
Mayor's calling for an end to prohibition,
bragging about the raid.

15:42.108 --> 15:45.028
Doesn't look good, you fraternizing
with the enemy the other night.

15:46.112 --> 15:47.155
I'm trying to help you.

15:48.239 --> 15:50.407
- Anything you want to tell me?
- Sure.

15:50.408 --> 15:52.409
I'm scared.

15:52.410 --> 15:53.952
You would be, too.

15:53.953 --> 15:55.454
Maybe you've forgotten,

15:55.455 --> 16:00.626
but Silvermane didn't get to where he is
by being calm and rational.

16:00.627 --> 16:03.838
He'll get rid of 50 if it means
he's sure he's got the one.

16:05.340 --> 16:08.051
It's too easy to get caught
in the crossfire when that happens.

16:09.094 --> 16:10.595
Try to remember that.

16:11.763 --> 16:13.223
If not for me...

16:16.810 --> 16:18.311
...then for you.

16:20.939 --> 16:22.856
[song ends]

16:22.857 --> 16:24.025
[exhales]

16:28.780 --> 16:30.448
[grunts]

16:32.909 --> 16:34.327
[creaking]

16:48.591 --> 16:49.883
[mysterious music playing]

16:49.884 --> 16:52.469
[Winston] Reilly. What are you doing here?

16:52.470 --> 16:53.804
Well, well, well.

16:53.805 --> 16:56.932
If it ain't Mr. Whiskers
searching for some cheese.

16:56.933 --> 16:59.309
And what the hell
is that supposed to mean?

16:59.310 --> 17:00.894
Your boss sent you out looking for supers,

17:00.895 --> 17:02.813
but here you are instead
covering your tracks,

17:02.814 --> 17:05.233
just like a rat, huh, Mr. Whiskers?

17:06.234 --> 17:08.485
You need to watch your mouth.

17:08.486 --> 17:10.112
- I have heard that, yes.
- I don't care

17:10.113 --> 17:12.114
if Silvermane hired you.

17:12.115 --> 17:13.574
I'm gonna find the rat,

17:13.575 --> 17:15.242
put him in the ground.

17:15.243 --> 17:18.620
Must sting,
not being trusted by the big boss anymore.

17:18.621 --> 17:21.039
He'll know he can trust me soon enough.

17:21.040 --> 17:23.542
Well, if you need a little help
from a professional in that effort,

17:23.543 --> 17:25.335
I could speed things up a bit.

17:25.336 --> 17:27.379
Maybe even share what I find.

17:27.380 --> 17:29.382
Not for nothing, of course.

17:30.383 --> 17:33.511
There's nothing worse
than a man that's only loyal to money.

17:38.808 --> 17:40.809
You find anything,

17:40.810 --> 17:43.812
I don't care whose favorite
lounge singer they are,

17:43.813 --> 17:45.440
you come to me first.

17:49.861 --> 17:51.571
Come on, Gio.

17:56.993 --> 17:59.412
♪ ♪

18:03.416 --> 18:04.666
[Robbie] And nobody could stop him.

18:04.667 --> 18:07.252
I mean, at one point,
he had half a dozen cops on him

18:07.253 --> 18:08.337
- whacking him with nightsticks...
- [door closes]

18:08.338 --> 18:09.922
...but he was indestructible.

18:09.923 --> 18:11.381
[Ben] Who?

18:11.382 --> 18:12.800
The guy from the picture.

18:12.801 --> 18:16.804
His name is Lonnie Lincoln.
Turns out he's got powers, too.

18:16.805 --> 18:19.932
I mean, cops were attacking him, but he
was swatting 'em off like it was nothing.

18:19.933 --> 18:22.142
And Flint. My God, man.

18:22.143 --> 18:24.895
- His hands were like boulders.
- Wait, wait, Flint?

18:24.896 --> 18:26.688
You're saying Flint Marko was there?

18:26.689 --> 18:28.398
He sure was.

18:28.399 --> 18:29.858
Say, can I borrow your darkroom?

18:29.859 --> 18:32.110
I was the only reporter there,
and the story is mine,

18:32.111 --> 18:33.612
as long as nobody poaches it.

18:33.613 --> 18:35.697
This could be my ticket back to the Bugle.

18:35.698 --> 18:36.782
[Janet] Here's something

18:36.783 --> 18:38.867
for your story.
Ben's hunch was right.

18:38.868 --> 18:42.372
Marko, Addison, and your Lincoln fella
were all POWs together.

18:44.082 --> 18:45.624
That photo Ben found

18:45.625 --> 18:47.334
was from the day they were rescued.

18:47.335 --> 18:48.794
Darkroom. Photos.

18:48.795 --> 18:50.088
Right now.

18:51.548 --> 18:52.966
[door opens]

18:55.301 --> 18:57.344
[creaking]

18:57.345 --> 18:59.179
Hunch, huh?

18:59.180 --> 19:03.517
We both know three POWs
from the same camp with super abilities

19:03.518 --> 19:04.601
isn't a coincidence.

19:04.602 --> 19:05.686
So what aren't you telling me?

19:05.687 --> 19:07.479
I can't get into it right now.

19:07.480 --> 19:08.564
Seriously?

19:08.565 --> 19:11.024
Suddenly you're not the only guy
in New York with powers

19:11.025 --> 19:12.901
and you can't get into it right now?

19:12.902 --> 19:14.611
- I have to fix something.
- No, no.

19:14.612 --> 19:16.071
None of this cryptic shit.

19:16.072 --> 19:18.115
- What the hell is going on?
- Silvermane

19:18.116 --> 19:20.075
hired me to find the rat in his crew,

19:20.076 --> 19:21.743
and it's Cat Hardy.

19:21.744 --> 19:23.287
The singer?

19:23.288 --> 19:25.372
- How do you know?
- She's been meeting with the mayor,

19:25.373 --> 19:27.040
and then he called for the raid.

19:27.041 --> 19:29.084
She's close with Flint,
and he served with Addison.

19:29.085 --> 19:30.627
- You sure?
- She's the only one

19:30.628 --> 19:32.296
who connects all the pieces.

19:32.297 --> 19:33.672
Wow, that is bold.

19:33.673 --> 19:35.173
Winston's only a step away,

19:35.174 --> 19:38.427
and if he finds out she was behind it,

19:38.428 --> 19:40.137
he'll kill her.

19:40.138 --> 19:41.931
[dramatic music playing]

19:43.892 --> 19:47.519
I need Vera Addison's room number
at the Geoffrey.

19:47.520 --> 19:49.397
I have a plan.

19:50.899 --> 19:53.443
- [indistinct chatter]
- [newsie] Extra, extra! Read all about it!

19:55.695 --> 19:58.322
Mayor cracking down on Hooverville!

19:58.323 --> 20:01.366
[tense music playing]

20:01.367 --> 20:03.285
Peanuts! Hot roasted peanuts here!

20:03.286 --> 20:05.288
♪ ♪

20:06.539 --> 20:08.541
[cool music playing]

20:11.711 --> 20:14.338
- [indistinct chatter]
- [vendor] Here you go, sir.

20:14.339 --> 20:15.714
[newsie] Extra!

20:15.715 --> 20:17.382
Three for a nickel!

20:17.383 --> 20:19.385
♪ ♪

20:29.771 --> 20:30.772
[horn honks]

20:32.565 --> 20:33.649
Extra!

20:33.650 --> 20:34.943
Read all about it.

20:35.944 --> 20:37.277
[vendor] Peanuts!

20:37.278 --> 20:39.029
Hot roasted peanuts here!

20:39.030 --> 20:40.530
[newsie] Murderers' Row ready for Boston!

20:40.531 --> 20:42.199
Read all about it!

20:42.200 --> 20:44.076
[tense music playing]

20:44.077 --> 20:46.120
Get your goddamn paws off me.

20:47.205 --> 20:49.499
Take it easy, pal.
I'm just trying to make a living.

20:51.376 --> 20:53.210
[newsie] Extra, extra!

20:53.211 --> 20:55.128
Read all about it!

20:55.129 --> 20:57.756
♪ ♪

20:57.757 --> 20:59.759
[cool music playing]

21:11.729 --> 21:14.982
I'd say "Don't be alarmed, Vera,"
but you don't appear to be.

21:14.983 --> 21:16.775
What do you want?

21:16.776 --> 21:19.194
Questions about your husband's last job.

21:19.195 --> 21:21.363
Specifically who hired him.

21:21.364 --> 21:22.990
I'm not interested in talking.

21:22.991 --> 21:25.367
I wasn't with the last guy,
and I'm not now.

21:25.368 --> 21:27.662
Even if you're the one in danger?

21:28.830 --> 21:30.748
[whistling]

21:33.710 --> 21:35.585
Let me make this easier for you.

21:35.586 --> 21:37.921
What if I told you I knew

21:37.922 --> 21:39.549
that it was Cat Hardy?

21:40.842 --> 21:43.468
If I know, then the others
will find out soon enough.

21:43.469 --> 21:46.054
Best thing you can do
is leave town, and fast.

21:46.055 --> 21:49.391
Silvermane will kill you
to get that information.

21:49.392 --> 21:51.518
Or pay me.

21:51.519 --> 21:54.771
I'm not stupid, mister.
You're here for her, not me.

21:54.772 --> 21:57.566
And if you're protecting her,
I've got a proposition for you.

21:57.567 --> 22:00.110
- What's that?
- You pay me

22:00.111 --> 22:02.237
a thousand dollars, and I'm gone.

22:02.238 --> 22:04.072
A thousand?

22:04.073 --> 22:05.949
I don't even know what that looks like.

22:05.950 --> 22:07.743
Mm.

22:07.744 --> 22:10.078
I bet Silvermane has that and then some.

22:10.079 --> 22:12.457
- I'll just tell him it's Cat myself.
- Slow down.

22:13.458 --> 22:15.751
I'll get you your money.

22:15.752 --> 22:18.755
You just stay out of trouble until then.

22:31.851 --> 22:33.602
[door closes]

22:33.603 --> 22:35.688
What a dump.

22:38.107 --> 22:39.816
Get the man a drink.

22:39.817 --> 22:42.944
Educate yourself. Try the Green Spot.

22:42.945 --> 22:45.155
Ten-year-old Irish pot still whiskey.

22:45.156 --> 22:48.326
Not what you're used to,
but I'm sure you can live with it.

22:53.372 --> 22:55.500
[exhales] It'll do.

22:56.834 --> 22:58.877
You must think I'm out of touch.

22:58.878 --> 23:00.378
[Ben] Money, power?

23:00.379 --> 23:05.175
Not a lot of it going around right now,
yet here you are in a castle tower.

23:05.176 --> 23:07.094
That's a testament to what you've built.

23:07.095 --> 23:11.516
It must be nice,
not having to look over your shoulder.

23:12.975 --> 23:17.437
So unconcerned with your possessions
'cause you have so little.

23:17.438 --> 23:21.234
You'd be surprised at how much people
will fight for what little they have.

23:23.444 --> 23:25.529
Do you know what entropy is, Reilly?

23:25.530 --> 23:28.365
The universe trends to disorder.

23:28.366 --> 23:29.867
Can't help itself.

23:30.910 --> 23:33.954
All you can do is fight
to keep the chaos from your door.

23:33.955 --> 23:35.789
[dark music playing]

23:35.790 --> 23:38.542
But like I said, you're lucky.

23:38.543 --> 23:41.419
You don't have anything
anyone wants to take. [laughs softly]

23:41.420 --> 23:43.631
Maybe not.

23:45.299 --> 23:48.553
But here's some friendly advice
all the same.

23:49.554 --> 23:51.847
Whoever the rat turns out to be,

23:51.848 --> 23:56.017
you can't be emotional about it,
even if it breaks your heart.

23:56.018 --> 23:59.437
And if someone should come to you
saying they have all the answers,

23:59.438 --> 24:01.065
know that they're lying.

24:03.860 --> 24:05.777
You know who it is, don't you?

24:05.778 --> 24:08.281
Doesn't matter what I know
until I can prove it.

24:10.283 --> 24:13.786
Well, the quicker you prove it,
the quicker they die.

24:14.787 --> 24:16.788
So, what are you waiting for?

24:16.789 --> 24:18.331
Thanks for the drink.

24:18.332 --> 24:21.376
It was just what I needed.

24:21.377 --> 24:22.628
[web squishes]

24:26.924 --> 24:28.175
[Robbie] This is an exclusive, Walters.

24:28.176 --> 24:30.343
The Bugle will be
the only ones to have it.

24:30.344 --> 24:33.513
No one else was there.
I am the only one with these.

24:33.514 --> 24:34.891
Mm-hmm.

24:40.646 --> 24:42.480
- [door closes]
- How you been? You look good.

24:42.481 --> 24:44.232
Well, you know, I'm getting by.

24:44.233 --> 24:45.984
- Say, listen, I was hoping--
- Oh, you still got the eye,

24:45.985 --> 24:47.235
I'll give you that.

24:47.236 --> 24:50.155
Well, I'm the same guy I always been.

24:50.156 --> 24:52.240
- Tell me the story.
- So,

24:52.241 --> 24:53.950
the cops came in frothing at the mouth.

24:53.951 --> 24:55.702
Now, uh, Lincoln,

24:55.703 --> 24:57.412
uh, he was just trying
to help his neighbor.

24:57.413 --> 24:59.289
He and Marko, they're both veterans.

24:59.290 --> 25:04.545
But now they're living in a Hooverville
with these mysterious powers.

25:07.506 --> 25:09.633
Superpowers. Ah.

25:09.634 --> 25:11.009
Just like The Spider.

25:11.010 --> 25:12.469
Before the asshole
decided to take a powder.

25:12.470 --> 25:14.971
Someone should've told him
a depression was coming. [laughs]

25:14.972 --> 25:18.350
- [laughs]
- Now you are bringing me two of them?

25:18.351 --> 25:19.893
The public can't get enough of this stuff.

25:19.894 --> 25:21.853
The papers will sell like crazy.

25:21.854 --> 25:23.772
Write it up.

25:23.773 --> 25:25.523
I want to go with this
in the next edition.

25:25.524 --> 25:28.068
Say, am I getting my old desk back
to write it at?

25:28.069 --> 25:30.779
Well, let's not run
before we can walk, huh?

25:30.780 --> 25:34.824
Um, for now, it'll be off the books,
you know, on the QT.

25:34.825 --> 25:36.993
But you keep bringing me more like this,

25:36.994 --> 25:40.580
and then we can talk about
bringing you back full-time.

25:40.581 --> 25:43.000
Like those old Spider days. [chuckles]

25:47.255 --> 25:49.799
- Good to see you again, Walters.
- [laughs]

25:51.300 --> 25:53.343
- Open or closed?
- Uh, closed.

25:53.344 --> 25:54.470
Okay.

25:57.139 --> 26:00.225
[Ben] So, I want you to be me. You know,
like one of those guys in the movies.

26:00.226 --> 26:02.519
You know, Bogie, Cagney, uh, Eddie G.

26:02.520 --> 26:04.980
You know, you c-can wear the hat,
you can smoke a cigarette.

26:04.981 --> 26:06.189
Y-You're cool.

26:06.190 --> 26:08.483
I want you to be cool. Hey!

26:08.484 --> 26:10.902
Focus. And quit casing my place.

26:10.903 --> 26:12.404
I ain't doing nothing.

26:12.405 --> 26:14.239
I need to rely on you, Frankie.

26:14.240 --> 26:15.740
Can I rely on you?

26:15.741 --> 26:17.243
I'm your man.

26:24.041 --> 26:25.459
[suspenseful music playing]

26:51.235 --> 26:53.029
[snoring]

27:09.754 --> 27:11.964
- [creaking]
- [suspenseful music playing]

27:23.309 --> 27:25.018
[mobster] Anything?

27:25.019 --> 27:27.021
He's been up there all night.

27:28.856 --> 27:30.858
[quirky music playing]

27:38.908 --> 27:41.659
[radio host] Calling all
junior detectives.

27:41.660 --> 27:44.079
Calling all junior detectives.

27:44.080 --> 27:47.541
Tonight's Mystery Hour is about to begin.

27:48.542 --> 27:50.544
[snoring]

28:14.610 --> 28:16.487
[muffled pulsing, warbling]

28:21.575 --> 28:22.910
[amplified clicking]

28:38.008 --> 28:40.010
[Silvermane snorts]

28:42.430 --> 28:44.432
[atmospheric music playing]

29:08.706 --> 29:11.000
♪ ♪

29:17.298 --> 29:18.299
[wind gusts]

29:21.093 --> 29:22.803
Boys!

29:24.555 --> 29:25.973
Hey, boss?

29:29.435 --> 29:32.645
- Well?
- Balcony door was open.

29:32.646 --> 29:34.230
No one's here.

29:34.231 --> 29:36.441
Think it was the wind.

29:36.442 --> 29:38.194
All right, well, check it again.

29:39.195 --> 29:41.197
[tense music playing]

29:52.541 --> 29:54.168
All clear, boss.

30:16.190 --> 30:18.192
[indistinct chatter]

30:30.829 --> 30:32.831
[footsteps approaching]

30:44.760 --> 30:46.010
[laughs softly]

30:46.011 --> 30:47.846
I taught you well.

30:53.811 --> 30:55.895
I should shoot you for running away.

30:55.896 --> 30:58.065
Well, how about kissing me
for coming back?

31:00.609 --> 31:02.611
[dramatic music playing]

31:11.704 --> 31:14.747
I've been so scared, Flint.

31:14.748 --> 31:17.750
I didn't know where you were,
what was happening to you.

31:17.751 --> 31:19.544
It's all right.

31:19.545 --> 31:21.672
I never should have run, but I'm back now.

31:22.673 --> 31:24.841
Something has happened.

31:24.842 --> 31:26.676
With Silvermane.

31:26.677 --> 31:28.261
I'll talk to him.

31:28.262 --> 31:29.762
Whatever it is, it can be fixed.

31:29.763 --> 31:31.347
No. No, I don't want to fix it.

31:31.348 --> 31:33.182
And I don't care about Silvermane.

31:33.183 --> 31:34.684
- What?
- I don't care about what he wants,

31:34.685 --> 31:36.603
I don't care about
what you think you owe him.

31:36.604 --> 31:39.023
I just want us to be together.

31:40.107 --> 31:41.858
If you love me...

31:41.859 --> 31:45.528
- Don't start with that--
- If you really love me,

31:45.529 --> 31:49.617
you won't ask any questions,
you'll just leave with me right now.

31:54.371 --> 31:55.997
Done.

31:55.998 --> 31:57.665
Really?

31:57.666 --> 31:59.167
Yeah.

31:59.168 --> 32:00.377
Pack a bag.

32:05.007 --> 32:06.592
[ominous music playing]

32:17.603 --> 32:19.021
- [Flint grunts]
- Are you okay?

32:20.522 --> 32:21.773
- No...
- What's the matter?

32:21.774 --> 32:23.608
Why did you turn away from me?

32:23.609 --> 32:25.069
Nothing. It's nothing.

32:28.030 --> 32:29.864
No! No, no, no. Stop, Flint.

32:29.865 --> 32:32.367
- No, Flint! Stop, please! Please.
- I can't!

32:32.368 --> 32:33.576
I can't!

32:33.577 --> 32:34.911
[tense music playing]

32:34.912 --> 32:36.664
There's no turning it off.

32:37.706 --> 32:39.290
There's no fixing me.

32:39.291 --> 32:41.668
- There has to be a way.
- [groans]

32:41.669 --> 32:43.086
We'll find a way.

32:43.087 --> 32:45.089
[panting]

32:48.300 --> 32:50.344
It's a fantasy.

32:52.346 --> 32:55.140
Kidding myself I could have this life.

32:56.141 --> 32:57.976
I could have you.

33:05.984 --> 33:07.361
- [crying]
- [door opens]

33:16.078 --> 33:17.662
You see this?

33:17.663 --> 33:19.914
They smashed up the cops.

33:19.915 --> 33:21.874
I'd have paid to see that.

33:21.875 --> 33:23.251
Reilly?

33:23.252 --> 33:24.878
He didn't leave all night.

33:27.631 --> 33:29.382
[Ben] That's right.

33:29.383 --> 33:31.677
Keep following me.

33:34.680 --> 33:36.806
I need you at The Alcove today.

33:36.807 --> 33:39.517
I want you to keep an eye
on Cat Hardy for me.

33:39.518 --> 33:42.645
And, uh, as promised.

33:42.646 --> 33:44.188
Look at me,

33:44.189 --> 33:46.524
- an honest working man.
- That's right.

33:46.525 --> 33:48.526
Now, if Ms. Hardy goes anywhere,

33:48.527 --> 33:49.944
I want to know about it.

33:49.945 --> 33:51.655
You got it, boss.

33:52.656 --> 33:55.283
That's right, folks.
Monsters in the streets.

33:55.284 --> 33:57.076
Get your copy while they last.

33:57.077 --> 34:00.372
Monsters on the loose.

34:01.373 --> 34:02.790
[Robbie] That...

34:02.791 --> 34:04.334
is not what I wrote.

34:05.335 --> 34:06.420
[mutters softly]

34:07.421 --> 34:10.798
"A routine sweep of a city Hooverville
revealed two violent monsters

34:10.799 --> 34:12.467
looking to harm all they came across..."

34:12.468 --> 34:14.469
I never called them monsters.

34:14.470 --> 34:16.763
"Only with the help
of our heroic police force

34:16.764 --> 34:19.056
did the residents escape
with their lives..."

34:19.057 --> 34:21.809
See, that, that is not what happened.

34:21.810 --> 34:24.605
He took my name
and put it on a bunch of lies.

34:25.606 --> 34:27.607
The pictures are great.

34:27.608 --> 34:29.358
What?

34:29.359 --> 34:31.736
[quirky music playing]

34:31.737 --> 34:33.446
[Ben] One hundred, two hundred,

34:33.447 --> 34:34.530
three hundred,

34:34.531 --> 34:36.032
four hundred, five hundred,

34:36.033 --> 34:37.742
six hundred, seven hundred, eight hundred,

34:37.743 --> 34:40.078
nine hundred, a thousand.

34:42.748 --> 34:44.040
A deal's a deal.

34:44.041 --> 34:46.418
You know what to do.

34:52.090 --> 34:54.675
Oh, look at that, shiny apples. Here.

34:54.676 --> 34:56.761
- Here you go. All right.
- [vendor] Oh. Grazie.

34:56.762 --> 34:58.764
[tense music playing]

35:00.891 --> 35:02.725
Hey, buddy, that was my foot.

35:02.726 --> 35:03.894
Mi scusi.

35:17.825 --> 35:20.159
- [Cat over phone] Hello?
- It's Ben. I need to see you.

35:20.160 --> 35:21.577
Why?

35:21.578 --> 35:23.789
I'll explain when I get there.
Just stay put.

35:28.669 --> 35:30.294
Someone wants to talk to you.

35:30.295 --> 35:31.880
Well, I'm busy. They can wait.

35:32.965 --> 35:35.258
Unhand my shoulder or lose your nose.

35:35.259 --> 35:36.717
It's the mayor.

35:36.718 --> 35:38.720
♪ ♪

35:40.222 --> 35:41.848
I want a line to The Spider.

35:41.849 --> 35:44.016
The guy from five years ago?

35:44.017 --> 35:45.977
I thought he was dead.

35:45.978 --> 35:48.145
I happen to know he's alive and well.

35:48.146 --> 35:50.106
Well, then, you know more than I do.

35:50.107 --> 35:51.983
Look, don't play dumb with me, pal.

35:51.984 --> 35:54.277
Back in the day,
you were always in the right place

35:54.278 --> 35:56.237
to snap a picture of The Spider.

35:56.238 --> 35:59.407
Whatever your deal is with him,
that's your business.

35:59.408 --> 36:02.159
You just tell your buddy
that I need to talk to him.

36:02.160 --> 36:04.161
Crime is out of control.

36:04.162 --> 36:06.831
People are scared,
and t-the city needs order.

36:06.832 --> 36:09.625
That why you're picking
a fight with Silvermane?

36:09.626 --> 36:12.253
Didn't he bankroll your first campaign?

36:12.254 --> 36:17.091
Silvermane is a ruthless criminal
who has squeezed this city long enough.

36:17.092 --> 36:20.011
Just get me in touch with The Spider.

36:20.012 --> 36:22.138
Make yourself a new friend.

36:22.139 --> 36:24.599
I can't wait.

36:24.600 --> 36:26.726
I believe in you, Ben Reilly.

36:26.727 --> 36:29.478
[Ben] Oh, my gosh, thank you so much.

36:29.479 --> 36:31.188
Where the hell you been?

36:31.189 --> 36:33.608
She took a cab to Penn Station
ten minutes ago.

36:33.609 --> 36:34.776
[exciting music playing]

36:37.237 --> 36:38.446
- [gasps]
- Just shush.

36:38.447 --> 36:40.073
Get out or you're coming with me.

36:44.536 --> 36:46.371
Penn Station on the double.

36:48.624 --> 36:50.459
♪ ♪

37:01.053 --> 37:02.387
Cat.

37:03.430 --> 37:04.847
Why are you here?

37:04.848 --> 37:07.642
You really aren't a very good detective,
are you?

37:07.643 --> 37:09.852
You don't strike me
as the kind of woman who runs.

37:09.853 --> 37:11.812
Maybe I lost my last reason
to stick around.

37:11.813 --> 37:14.273
What do you say we cut the fancy talk?

37:14.274 --> 37:17.193
You found Addison through Flint
and paid him to bomb Silvermane's mansion.

37:17.194 --> 37:19.528
You tipped off Morris
about the booze shipment.

37:19.529 --> 37:23.366
You're Silvermane's rat.
The only thing I don't know is why.

37:23.367 --> 37:25.284
You know, you boys are all the same.

37:25.285 --> 37:29.080
You come up with your own little stories
and you make everyone else fit them.

37:29.081 --> 37:32.083
Silvermane treats me like a damn doll,
Flint thinks I'm afraid of him

37:32.084 --> 37:33.918
and you think I'm a killer.

37:33.919 --> 37:37.755
I am done with people telling me
who I am and what I get to do.

37:37.756 --> 37:39.924
- You ask me why I'm leaving?
- [Winston] Hey, Reilly.

37:39.925 --> 37:41.927
[suspenseful music playing]

37:43.345 --> 37:45.596
There you are.

37:45.597 --> 37:48.141
And look, a bonus.

37:49.184 --> 37:52.645
I guess I am the luckiest guy in New York.

37:52.646 --> 37:53.896
[sighs] Man.

37:53.897 --> 37:56.274
I should've known you were in it together.

37:57.275 --> 37:59.152
Now the boss can take care of both of you.

38:04.157 --> 38:05.742
Move.

38:12.040 --> 38:14.334
[train rattling on tracks]

38:30.559 --> 38:32.393
♪ ♪

38:32.394 --> 38:35.479
You know, dick, I got to give you credit.

38:35.480 --> 38:37.606
You came close.

38:37.607 --> 38:41.318
Too bad you couldn't get
the Addison widow out of town.

38:41.319 --> 38:44.155
I only had to slap her around
a little bit to get the truth.

38:44.156 --> 38:45.782
What a guy.

38:47.492 --> 38:50.912
Yeah, well, a prick to the end, huh?

38:52.205 --> 38:54.458
Might be the only thing I like about you.

39:00.047 --> 39:01.673
[engine turns off]

39:10.557 --> 39:12.559
♪ ♪

39:21.777 --> 39:25.362
[Winston] I caught them both
trying to skip town, boss.

39:25.363 --> 39:27.031
It looks like Reilly was in on it.

39:27.032 --> 39:28.867
The guy with all the answers.

39:33.080 --> 39:34.288
[gasps]

39:34.289 --> 39:37.334
You didn't think
you'd be seeing her again, did you?

39:38.335 --> 39:40.377
This is Addison's widow.

39:40.378 --> 39:43.255
She's also the only person who knows
who hired her dearly deceased husband.

39:43.256 --> 39:46.301
She didn't want to talk, but, uh...

39:48.512 --> 39:50.262
...she came around.

39:50.263 --> 39:51.723
Right? [chuckles]

39:53.433 --> 39:56.144
Hurry up, unless you want
to join your husband.

39:57.187 --> 39:58.688
- This is a--
- Quiet.

40:01.149 --> 40:03.859
Let's hear what the widow has to say.

40:03.860 --> 40:06.153
He told me it was Cat Hardy.

40:06.154 --> 40:08.990
That she paid him a thousand dollars
to burn down your mansion.

40:10.826 --> 40:12.368
[Winston] What'd I tell you, huh?

40:12.369 --> 40:15.372
You can dress up a stray dog
however you like, it'll still bite you.

40:16.414 --> 40:17.791
So you've said.

40:19.876 --> 40:21.253
It's not true.

40:22.254 --> 40:23.504
- It's not me.
- [Winston chuckles]

40:23.505 --> 40:25.674
Lying to the end, huh?

40:26.675 --> 40:29.552
I always knew
it was just a matter of time with you.

40:29.553 --> 40:32.138
It's a good story, I'll give you that.

40:32.139 --> 40:33.639
You got proof?

40:33.640 --> 40:36.142
Yeah. Show them.

40:36.143 --> 40:37.769
Come on.

40:42.899 --> 40:45.985
She couldn't quite manage to blow it all.

40:45.986 --> 40:47.695
Too bad, huh?

40:47.696 --> 40:49.364
[laughs]

40:57.789 --> 40:59.124
[laughs]

41:01.793 --> 41:03.461
[stifled laugh]

41:05.046 --> 41:07.423
Where does your money come from, Winston?

41:07.424 --> 41:09.550
[suspenseful music playing]

41:09.551 --> 41:11.385
From you.

41:11.386 --> 41:13.471
That's right. From me.

41:14.472 --> 41:17.058
And did you know that I mark all my bills?

41:20.604 --> 41:23.857
A different spot for every schmuck
on my payroll.

41:25.692 --> 41:27.611
Guess where I mark yours.

41:29.613 --> 41:31.864
What?

41:31.865 --> 41:33.408
That's not possible.

41:37.746 --> 41:40.790
There's nothing worse than a man
who's only loyal to money.

41:41.833 --> 41:43.584
You son of a bitch.

41:43.585 --> 41:45.461
[Vera] I bet Silvermane has that
and then some.

41:45.462 --> 41:47.297
Maybe I'll go talk to him.

41:48.340 --> 41:52.259
[Ben] Crafty bastard
marks all of his bills.

41:52.260 --> 41:53.595
You set me up?

41:54.596 --> 41:55.931
[Silvermane] People lie, Reilly.

41:56.932 --> 41:58.934
Only money tells the truth.

42:01.019 --> 42:03.979
It was him. He threatened
to kill me if I said otherwise.

42:03.980 --> 42:06.398
You lying bitch. I'll rip your goddamn--

42:06.399 --> 42:07.943
- [gunshot]
- [gasps]

42:15.033 --> 42:16.242
[clears throat]

42:16.243 --> 42:17.994
[gun cocks]

42:21.623 --> 42:24.209
You good with a shovel, Reilly?

42:25.669 --> 42:27.378
Why?

42:27.379 --> 42:30.048
We'll be needing another grave.

42:32.801 --> 42:34.803
[atmospheric music playing]

43:02.831 --> 43:04.833
♪ ♪

43:32.861 --> 43:34.863
♪ ♪

44:02.891 --> 44:04.893
♪ ♪

44:32.921 --> 44:34.923
♪ ♪
